SRC/bks -- Brickstop, as built for OS-9/68000=============================================ORIG holds the post as comp.sources.games carried it (bs.c, with BillRandle's BSD changes).  It is built with BSD defined, and bs.c differs fromthe post only inside #ifdef OSK:  - doze() sleeps with tsleep() in 256ths of a second, for select().  - pending keystrokes are counted with _gs_rdy(0), for ioctl(FIONREAD).  - random() and srandom() are rand() and srand(), from /dd/LIB/rand.r.  - the high scores live in /dd/GAMES/BKS/hiscores.  OS-9's open() takes    no O_CREAT, so the file is made with creat() the first time; the name    stored is $USER, for cuserid().The module is named bks, the post's archive name, because this disk's`bs' is Battleships.  ESC, which the menu calls pause, runs a shell escapethrough system() -- and OS-9's terminal driver takes ESC as end of file, soit does nothing here.